From: cliffhall <cliff@futurescale.com>
Date: Tue, 29 Sep 2026 01:48:42 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] fix(issue-triage): harden the PR close loop and scope the
 step 0 close rule

Copilot round 1 on #4906:
- the manifest uses '-' for 'no issue', because read collapses adjacent tabs
  and an empty field shifted the reason into the issue column
- class slugs are defined in the table; the loop whitelists them, skips
  'security', and stops on anything unknown instead of closing it
- the backlog sweep's close label and #4875 reference (SWEEP_LABEL, SWEEP_REF)
  are part of the loop, and the step 0 issue closes take the same two
- step 0's close rule covers only rows whose Action is Close, never a
  security report

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: cliffhall <cliff@futurescale.com>
